  <reporting-org ref="GB-GOV-1" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UK - Foreign, Commonwealth Development Office (FCDO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting enhanced transparency in extractive industries gopvernance and promoting civic space through PWYP and the EITI.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the project is to promote transparency in the extractive industries in Niger through the implementation of the 20/25 vision and the protection of civic space. 

To achieve this overall objective and the specific objectives of this project, ROTAB intends to: Educate, raise awareness and inform the public, local communities and people with disabilities on their rights in relation to mining and oil exploitation through the 2023 EITI standard (requirement N&#xb0;2). Indeed, it is time to capitalize on experiences in the use of fees retroceded to municipalities through the collection of data from 2018-2023. For the proper participation of civil society actors who sit in the GMC EITI will strengthen their capacities on PWYP&apos;s Vision 2025 and other transparency standards in Niger. A follow-up plan for the continuous recommendations in the Niger EITI reports will be developed and executed. 

This project will be implemented in accordance with the principles of results-based management and the participatory approach with the beneficiaries as well as the use of new technology and digital technology through platforms.</narrative>
  </description>
